            <ArticleTitle>Breaking the (un)sound barrier: filaggrin is a major gene for atopic dermatitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1200-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have recently shown that loss-of-function mutations in the filaggrin gene, carried by about 10% of people of European ethnicity, cause ichthyosis vulgaris and are strong predisposing factors for atopic dermatitis and asthma secondary to atopic dermatitis. These results demonstrate a prominent role for the epidermal barrier in atopic disease and have important implications for the study of complex traits.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
